// Phase 10 audit round-12, finding 2: calling a method declared without a
// body must be a compile error. Body-less non-native functions are skipped
// at backend registration (they have nothing to compile), yet the resolver
// still bound calls to them — codegen then silently skipped the call opcode
// and the expression evaluated to stale memory. The backend now rejects the
// call at the registration miss instead of emitting wrong code.
class C {
    public int m();
}

int main() {
    C c = new C();
    return c.m();
}
